Backport of apache/guacamole-server commit
6f4b4516350605f7a3135ef7db18b367d4188ae9 (GUACAMOLE-2270):
https://github.com/apache/guacamole-server/commit/6f4b4516350605f7a3135ef7db18b367d4188ae9
Upstream patch SHA-256: ce137cf5270dbc693a9c4692871e051781e46999554de38cd975313e3bb64998

guac_display_dup() held last_frame.lock and then took pending_frame.lock
through guac_display_layer_get_bounds(), the reverse of the frame flush
order. A user joining while the first frame flushed could deadlock both
threads. Applies unchanged to the released 1.6.0 display.c.

--- a/src/libguac/display.c
+++ b/src/libguac/display.c
@@ -255,8 +255,14 @@
 
         const guac_layer* layer = current->layer;
 
-        guac_rect layer_bounds;
-        guac_display_layer_get_bounds(current, &layer_bounds);
+        /* Determine layer bounds from last frame, NOT pending frame as
+         * provided by guac_display_layer_get_bounds() */
+        guac_rect layer_bounds = {
+            .left   = 0,
+            .top    = 0,
+            .right  = current->last_frame.width,
+            .bottom = current->last_frame.height
+        };
 
         int width = guac_rect_width(&layer_bounds);
         int height = guac_rect_height(&layer_bounds);
